{"v":1,"seq":2,"id":"01M7TK6GX0T1146Q3MF5ZDJ036","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"user","text":"I'm building trip-planner, a small web app for our hiking trips. I want the map to work without signal. What are my options?","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:0:791a672974e4a01e"}
{"v":1,"seq":3,"id":"01M7TK6GX0C8D2BWYR5TH2J090","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","text":"Three realistic options:\n\n1. Cache the raster tiles in the browser (Cache Storage, served by a service worker).\n2. Ship vector tiles as one PMTiles file per region.\n3. Pre-render one static image per day of the trip.\n\nWhich one fits depends on the map library you already use and on how large an area a trip covers.","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:1:2bfbe023191befbd"}
{"v":1,"seq":4,"id":"01M7TK6GX0NBAXDBWKXWRM7996","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"user","text":"The app already uses Leaflet with raster tiles. A trip covers a small area. What's the least work?","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:2:80da639e9151753f"}
{"v":1,"seq":5,"id":"01M7TK6GX00D6ZZYJCRRXBD6T0","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","text":"Then cache the raster tiles. Take the bounding box of the itinerary plus a margin, zoom levels 10 to 15, and store the tiles in Cache Storage; the service worker answers from the cache first. Expect about 30 MB per trip.\n\nCheck the tile provider's usage policy first: many forbid bulk downloads. Use one that allows it, or your own tile server.","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:3:5c3f371e44c170f8"}
{"v":1,"seq":6,"id":"01M7TK6GX03KS6XDJWJ943GCVR","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"user","text":"OK, let's do that. Cap it at 40 MB per trip and show progress while it downloads.","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:4:742bc0ce601aa660"}
{"v":1,"seq":7,"id":"01M7TK6GX02FKZ7EY40C2AMBS2","at":"2026-11-19T19:05:40Z","leg":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","text":"Plan:\n\n- A \"Save for offline\" button on the trip page.\n- List the tiles for the bounding box, zoom 10 to 15; stop adding zoom levels when the estimate passes 40 MB.\n- Download four at a time, with a progress bar and a cancel button.\n- The service worker serves `/tiles/` from the cache first, then the network.\n- A \"Remove offline map\" button that deletes the trip's cache.","source":"connector","app":"chatgpt","key":"conn:chatgpt:offline-maps-for-the-itinerary:5:64b9e7166c2fb38f"}
